Subject: Gambatte: Game Boy Color infrared port (RP, FF56) over the same netplay room (v5ir)
Series-Step: 2/5 (gambatte link v5irh3)
Origin: hanbang (this project); record name hanbang_gb_ir_v5ir_from_v4bw.diff
요약: 게임보이 컬러 적외선 포트(FF56)를 같은 넷플레이 방으로 이음 — 포켓몬 금·은·크리스탈 이상한 소포, 핀볼 점수 보내기, 카드 GB 카드 뿅!.

While a game keeps its IR port on, each side sends 20-byte 'I' reports (its Game Boy time in 4194304 Hz
units, LED on/off, port on/off, "reading" flag). When both ports are on and both sides read RP, the two meet once at a
barrier (the host decides which two stops belong together) and from then the two Game Boy times are tied. A Game Boy
reading RP at time t sees the other LED as it was at t - 4096 units (0.98 ms each way); if the other side's reports do not
reach that far yet it waits there with its game paused (at most 3 s). A long pulse (>= 256 units) stays visible 128 units
after it ends (the Mystery Gift hello). A port that is on but not read for two frames counts as "not listening", so a
menu that leaves the port on (Pokemon Pinball after a send) does not freeze the other side. The pad is re-read during
long waits so a short press is not lost. Cores without this patch ignore the 20-byte packets, so a half-updated pair only
loses the infrared feature (no freeze).

Hooks: FF56 read/write in Memory (CGB only), SerialIO::irWrite / irRead / irTick, checkSerial calls irTick.

