+/* Hanbang v5ir (2026-10-26): Game Boy Color infrared (RP, FF56) over the same netplay room.
+ * Each Game Boy keeps running its own game; while a game has its IR port on, each side sends
+ * reports (its own time in 4194304 Hz units, LED on/off, port on/off). When both ports are on,
+ * the two meet once (barrier: each stops at its next RP read until the other one's stop is
+ * known) and from then the two Game Boy times are tied. A Game Boy reading RP at time t sees the
+ * other LED as it was at t - HB_IR_LAG, and if the other side's reports do not reach that far
+ * yet, it waits there with its game paused (conservative lockstep, only while both ports are on).
+ * The lag is like a longer distance between the two: Pokemon Gold/Silver/Crystal Mystery Gift
+ * waits 256 timer ticks (11.7 ms) for each answer and measures bits by the time between edges,
+ * so a fixed 2 ms delay each way is still well inside it. Packets are 20 bytes ('I'), so cores
+ * without this ignore them (old cores never see light, as before). */
